2026-09-27T12:05:48.4822666Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4822857Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4823134Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4823391Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4823472Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4823687Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4823799Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4823950Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4824688Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4824903Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4825017Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4825275Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4825446Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4825573Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4825936Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4826266Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4826899Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4827394Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4827499Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4827896Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4828400Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4828665Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4828946Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4829328Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4829407Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4829589Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4829702Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4830936Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4832226Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4899620Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4900566Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4901497Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4902106Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4902656Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4903097Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4903502Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4903612Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4903848Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4903990Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4905398Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4906572Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4907243Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4908190Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:48.4908432Z 
